    "question": "Two solid cylinders $A$ and $B$ are made of the same material and have the same mass and length. Cylinder $A$ is solid with radius $R$, while cylinder $B$ is a hollow tube with inner radius $r$ and outer radius $R_o$. If $R_o = 2r$, the ratio of the torsional rigidity of hollow cylinder $B$ to that of solid cylinder $A$ ($C_B / C_A$) is:",
